From cccf2477fa2337e2e0188136c8929ded1c9f0787 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:10:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] worker-placement: a no_eligible_worker card tells
 its owner the repin command once per revision

Ruling 9 of the overflow plan keeps a card no pool worker can run queued and fenced with no automatic return
to origin. It used to wait silently. Now the origin posts one comment (missing labels + the exact
'hermes kanban move <id> --runs-on machine:<origin>' command) and a worker_repin_notice event its origin chat
receives (gateway + TUI notifiers), once per card revision (required labels + run count, not sync_version, which
every reserve bumps). It runs on every reserve reply, so cards already queued get it on the next pass. The
stuck summary lists them as 'waiting for a manual repin' and no longer blames the lease. Nothing repins.
