-Workers always win. The Board reserves the origin hub for a portable card only when **every** compatible member of the origin's *configured* pool (never the request subset) is known, fresh and refused solely for pressure (score >= .85) or full slots, AND the hub's reported measured CPU busy is fresh (conservative end within 15 s) and strictly below the operator's threshold, AND hub capacity/memory/drain allow it, AND no other hub overflow reservation is outstanding, AND the sample's conservative start is after the last hub overflow grant. Unknown, stale, held, draining or offline workers veto overflow and the card queues. Zero compatible workers queues with `no_eligible_worker`: the automatic structural origin repin was removed (only the explicit owner repin clears the fence). Prior runs, host-bound cards and running leases are never moved.
+Workers always win. The Board reserves the origin hub for a portable card only when **every** compatible member of the origin's *configured* pool (never the request subset) is known, fresh and refused solely for pressure (score >= .85) or full slots, AND the hub's reported measured CPU busy is fresh (conservative end within 15 s) and strictly below the operator's threshold, AND hub capacity/memory/drain allow it, AND no other hub overflow reservation is outstanding, AND the sample's conservative start is after the last hub overflow grant. Unknown, stale, held, draining or offline workers veto overflow and the card queues. Zero compatible workers queues with `no_eligible_worker`: the automatic structural origin repin was removed (only the explicit owner repin clears the fence). The origin then posts one owner notice per card revision (`hermes_cli/kanban_repin_notice.py`): a comment naming the missing labels and the exact `hermes kanban move <id> --runs-on machine:<origin> --reason "no pool worker can run it"` command, plus a `worker_repin_notice` event its origin chat receives; the dispatcher stuck summary lists such cards as "waiting for a manual repin" instead of a stall. Nothing repins automatically. Prior runs, host-bound cards and running leases are never moved.
 
